CC   TAG2 is a HAT-like DNA transposon; it is flanked by 18-bp
CC   terminal inverted repeats. Its copies are flanked by 8-bp
CC   target site duplications generated upon transposition in the
CC   genome. TAG2p transposase is encoded by 2 exons.
